/*!
   \qmlmodule org.kde.kirigamiaddons.delegates
   \title Kirigami Addons Delegates QML Types
   \brief Delegates for lists and grids in Kirigami applications.

   Import the module with an alias in a QML file that displays a collection:

   \qml
   import org.kde.kirigamiaddons.delegates as Delegates
   \endqml

   \section1 Displaying a list

   Use \l RoundedItemDelegate for a list or grid item that opens another
   page or selects an item. It provides a rounded background for hover,
   focus, and selection states. When it is the direct delegate of a
   \l ListView or \l GridView, it uses the view to size itself and highlight
   the current item.

   \image roundeditemdelegate.png Rounded delegates in a list

   \qml
   import QtQuick
   import org.kde.kirigamiaddons.delegates as Delegates

   ListView {
       id: foldersView
       model: ["Inbox", "Archive"]

       delegate: Delegates.RoundedItemDelegate {
           required property int index
           required property string modelData

           text: modelData
           icon.name: "folder"
           onClicked: foldersView.currentIndex = index
       }
   }
   \endqml

   In a drag and drop workflow, the view's delegate can be an \c Item that
   stays in the list or grid while its child \l RoundedItemDelegate is
   reparented during a drag. The child does not receive the view's attached
   properties automatically. Bind \c {listView: wrapper.ListView} or
   \c {gridView: wrapper.GridView} to retain the built-in sizing and
   highlighting, or set those properties on the child explicitly.

   \section1 Adding a subtitle or extra content

   The default \l DefaultContentItem shows the delegate's icon and text.
   Replace \c contentItem with \l SubtitleContentItem to add a second
   line. Pass the containing delegate through \c itemDelegate so the
   content uses its text, icon, font, and enabled state:

   \qml
   Delegates.RoundedItemDelegate {
       id: messageDelegate
       text: i18nc("@title", "Project update")
       icon.name: "mail-message"

       contentItem: Delegates.SubtitleContentItem {
           itemDelegate: messageDelegate
           subtitle: i18nc("@info", "Received today")
       }
   }
   \endqml

   For a more specialized layout, place \l DefaultContentItem inside a
   \c RowLayout with other controls and assign the layout to
   \c contentItem.

   \section1 Choices, unread items, and trees

   Use \l CheckDelegate for an independent on/off choice and
   \l RadioDelegate for a choice in a group. Both show an indicator and
   expose the inherited \c checked and \c toggled members. Put radio
   delegates in a \c ButtonGroup when only one choice may be selected.
   Store the checked state in the model when delegates may be recreated as
   the user scrolls.

   \l IndicatorItemDelegate adds an accent bar for an unread item. It is
   intended as a direct \l ListView delegate; set its required \c unread
   property. The view supplies \c index from the model. Use
   \l RoundedTreeDelegate with a
   \c KDescendantsProxyModel to show expandable tree rows in a
   \l ListView. It expects the descendant level and expansion roles from
   that model.

   \sa RoundedItemDelegate
   \sa CheckDelegate
   \sa RadioDelegate
   \sa SubtitleContentItem
   \sa IndicatorItemDelegate
   \sa RoundedTreeDelegate
 */
